{
  "about": "veffgraindelay: a grain delay, in the unit's own lists of effects (sounds and master) and on fx train's wagons. Grains read from a stereo delay line, each with its own place and pitch. Knobs: pitch (-24..+24 semitones, fine near 0), spray (0..500 ms), feedback (0..95), mix; with shift held: delay (2/1..1/64 of the tempo, then 0..1000 ms), freq (the grain rate, 1..150 Hz), random (random pitch), spread, and reverse. Starts as an octave-up shimmer on the eighth note. Stands on delay; changes no place of the firmware; needs the base.",
